# Frontend context menus & selects

For any dropdown, overflow menu, status picker, or action menu in the frontend:

- Use `ContextMenu` from `frontend/src/components/ui` for action menus (edit / delete / add…).
- Use `Select` from `frontend/src/components/ui` for single-value pickers (status, type, etc.).
- Both are custom UI. Do **not** use native `<select>`, browser `<option>` lists, or OS context menus for product UI.
- Do **not** invent a one-off absolute-positioned menu when `ContextMenu` already covers it.
- Menu items must use `cursor-pointer` (built into `ContextMenu` / `Select`).
- Keep styling on our design tokens: `border-line`, `bg-surface`, `rounded-2xl`, `shadow-[var(--shadow-panel)]`.
